  "description": "DeCUR is a multimodal self-supervised learning method that decouples common and unique representations across modalities, enhancing both intra- and inter-modal learning. It extends Barlow Twins with a loss design for modality decoupling and optionally integrates deformable attention for modality-informative feature learning. Evaluated on SAR-optical, RGB-DEM, and RGB-depth scenarios, DeCUR achieves state-of-the-art results in both multimodal and modality-missing settings.",
  "sci:doi": "10.48550/arXiv.2309.05300",
